-- title:
--   History $\sigma$-algebra $\mathcal H_t$ with external randomization
-- statement:
--   The information available when patient $t+1$ is allocated: the $\sigma$-algebra generated by an external randomization $\mathcal G$ (used for random tie-breaking and random consideration sets) and by the pairs $(u^s,Y^{s+1}_{u^s})$, $s<t$, of past allocations and observations. The prior parameters are known constants. This is the history $\mathcal H_t$ of p. 7 together with $\mathcal G$.
-- source:
--   Chick, Gans & Yapar, Bayesian Sequential Learning for Clinical Trials of Multiple Correlated Medical Interventions, SSRN preprint 3184758 (version of August 31, 2020), p. 7 (§1.3, history H_t)

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_CPDETrial_obs
open MeasureTheory ProbabilityTheory Filter Topology
open scoped NNReal ENNReal

namespace CPDETrial

/-- **The history σ-algebra `H_t`, with external randomization.**
Chick, Gans & Yapar, *Bayesian Sequential Learning for Clinical Trials of Multiple Correlated
Medical Interventions*, SSRN preprint 3184758 (version of August 31, 2020), §1.3, p. 7: "`H_t = {µ⁰, Σ⁰, u⁰, Y¹_{u⁰}, u¹, Y²_{u¹}, …, u^{t−1}, Y^t_{u^{t−1}}}` … the
history of a trial up to time `t`".

`hist 𝓖 θ ε u t` is generated by the external randomization `𝓖` (random tie-breaks, random
consideration sets) and by the pairs `(u^s, Y^{s+1}_{u^s})` for `s < t`. The parameters
`µ⁰, Σ⁰, Λ` are fixed (known, Assumption 1(i)) and generate nothing.

**Formalization Note.** `𝓖` is the `σ`-algebra of auxiliary randomness, assumed independent of
`(θ, ε)` in `TrialModel`; it is what the paper's "ties broken randomly" (p. 11) and the random
consideration sets of App. B.10 (p. ec12) need. -/
noncomputable def hist {M : ℕ} {Ω : Type*} (𝓖 : MeasurableSpace Ω) (θ : Ω → EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin M))
    (ε : ℕ → Fin M → Ω → ℝ) (u : ℕ → Ω → Fin M) (t : ℕ) : MeasurableSpace Ω :=
  𝓖 ⊔ ⨆ (s : ℕ) (_ : s < t),
    MeasurableSpace.comap (fun ω => (u s ω, obs θ ε u s ω)) inferInstance

end CPDETrial


